ok, let's do it pern and prisma stack
Alright, let's build a secure and scalable application using the PERN (PostgreSQL, Express, React, Node.js) stack with Prisma as our ORM tool to manage the database. We'll integrate JWT-based authentication and handle tokens on the client side.

Project Overview
We'll create a simple application with the following features:

Authentication using JWT (login and token validation).

Server-side API with Prisma for database operations.

Client-side React application that fetches data and handles the JWT.

1. Set Up the Backend (Express + Prisma)
a. Install dependencies
bash
mkdir pern-prisma-app
cd pern-prisma-app
npm init -y
npm install express prisma @prisma/client jsonwebtoken bcrypt cors dotenv
b. Set up Prisma
Initialize Prisma:

bash
npx prisma init
Configure the prisma/schema.prisma file with the following:

prisma
datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
  url      = env("DATABASE_URL")
}

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
}

model User {
  id       Int     @id @default(autoincrement())
  email    String  @unique
  password String
}
Set up your PostgreSQL database and provide the connection URL in .env:

dotenv
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://username:password@localhost:5432/mydatabase
Generate Prisma Client:

bash
npx prisma generate
Migrate the database:

bash
npx prisma migrate dev --name init
c. Create the Express server
Create a server.js file:

javascript
const express = require('express');
const prisma = require('@prisma/client').PrismaClient;
const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');
const bcrypt = require('bcrypt');
const cors = require('cors');
const dotenv = require('dotenv');
dotenv.config();

const app = express();
const prismaClient = new prisma();

app.use(express.json());
app.use(cors());

// Register user
app.post('/register', async (req, res) => {
  const { email, password } = req.body;
  const hashedPassword = await bcrypt.hash(password, 10);
  try {
    const newUser = await prismaClient.user.create({
      data: { email, password: hashedPassword },
    });
    res.json(newUser);
  } catch (error) {
    res.status(400).json({ error: 'User already exists' });
  }
});

// Login user and generate JWT
app.post('/login', async (req, res) => {
  const { email, password } = req.body;
  const user = await prismaClient.user.findUnique({ where: { email } });
  if (!user) return res.status(404).json({ error: 'User not found' });

  const isValidPassword = await bcrypt.compare(password, user.password);
  if (!isValidPassword) return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Invalid credentials' });

  const token = jwt.sign({ userId: user.id }, process.env.JWT_SECRET, { expiresIn: '1h' });
  res.json({ token });
});

// Verify JWT middleware
const authenticate = (req, res, next) => {
  const token = req.headers.authorization?.split(' ')[1];
  if (!token) return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Unauthorized' });

  try {
    const decoded = jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET);
    req.userId = decoded.userId;
    next();
  } catch {
    res.status(401).json({ error: 'Unauthorized' });
  }
};

// Protected route
app.get('/protected', authenticate, async (req, res) => {
  const user = await prismaClient.user.findUnique({ where: { id: req.userId } });
  res.json(user);
});

app.listen(5000, () => console.log('Server running on http://localhost:5000'));
