Scenario: Set up a CI/CD pipeline that builds Docker images, runs tests, and deploys them to Kubernetes.

Step 1: Define the Pipeline Use GitHub Actions to automate build, test, and deployment. Create .github/workflows/deploy.yml:

yaml
name: CI/CD Pipeline

on:
  push:
    branches:
      - main

jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      # Checkout Code
      - name: Checkout Code
        uses: actions/checkout@v2

      # Build Backend
      - name: Build Backend Docker Image
        run: |
          docker build -t backend:latest ./backend

      # Build Frontend
      - name: Build Frontend Docker Image
        run: |
          docker build -t frontend:latest ./client

  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      # Run Backend Tests
      - name: Run Backend Tests
        run: |
          cd backend
          npm install
          npm test

      # Run Frontend Tests
      - name: Run Frontend Tests
        run: |
          cd client
          npm install
          npm test

  deploy:
    needs: [build, test]
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      # Configure Kubernetes CLI
      - name: Configure kubectl
        uses: azure/setup-kubectl@v1
        with:
          version: 'latest'

      # Deploy to Kubernetes
      - name: Apply Manifests
        run: |
          kubectl apply -f k8s/backend-deployment.yml
          kubectl apply -f k8s/frontend-deployment.yml
Step 2: Push Logs to Loki Include a step to forward pipeline logs to Loki:

yaml
      - name: Forward Logs to Loki
